  "html": "<h2>Information here, controls over there</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Both webs in this story split one thing in two: what a loan is, and what you can do with it.</p>\n<div class=\"split\">\n  <p class=\"era\">1997</p>\n  <figure class=\"half\"><img src=\"media/loans-data.png\" alt=\"Her loans page: loan numbers, book numbers, titles and due dates, with no links.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption><b>Information:</b> her loans page. Numbers, titles, due dates.</figcaption></figure>\n  <p class=\"gap\"><span>Ana joins them, with a sticky note and her own typing</span></p>\n  <figure class=\"half\"><img src=\"media/forms-html.png\" alt=\"forms.html at RENEW A LOAN, the same for every loan.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption><b>Controls:</b> forms.html. Every operation, for every loan.</figcaption></figure>\n  <p class=\"era\">Today</p>\n  <figure class=\"half\">\n<pre><code>GET /loans/3310\nAccept: application/json\n\n{ \"id\": 3310, \"title\": \"The Hobbit\",\n  \"author\": \"J. R. R. Tolkien\",\n  \"due\": \"2026-11-12\", \"renewals\": 0,\n  \"standing\": \"hold waiting\" }</code></pre>\n    <figcaption><b>Information:</b> the loan, as JSON. Nothing in it says what it allows.</figcaption></figure>\n  <p class=\"gap\"><span>The agent joins them, reading prose and guessing</span></p>\n  <figure class=\"half\"><img src=\"media/openapi-renew.png\" alt=\"Swagger UI's renew operation: offered while the book is out, renewed fewer than three times, and no one's hold is waiting.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption><b>Controls:</b> the OpenAPI document. Renew, for every loan, its rule in prose.</figcaption></figure>\n</div>\n<p class=\"lead\">Neither half knows about the other. The client joins them every time, and learns it joined them wrong only after the call: 409.</p>\n<p class=\"note\">Next: Fielding's name for keeping the two together.</p>\n"
}
